{"_v":1,"id":"rain-2010","bd":{"positive":7,"mixed":3,"negative":2},"rv":[{"cn":"Terry Teachout","o":"The Wall Street Journal","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.wsj.com/articles/SB1000142405274870446130457621611048856250","d":"2011-03-09","q":"The four young Liverpudlians who make up Rain are such dead ringers for the original Beatles that watching them is like peering through a time machine."},{"cn":"Frank Scheck","o":"The Hollywood Reporter","s":76,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/review/rain-tribute-beatles-broadway-theater-32763","q":"Although purists might sneer at this concert/theatrical experience, there’s no denying that, as cover bands go, this is one of the best."},{"cn":"Mark Kennedy","o":"Associated Press","s":72,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.google.com/hostednews/canadianpress/article/ALeqM5iafSQYBMWdHSdHx0ti53-RmZknzw?docId=4946154","q":"But after a show like this, the only impression that is left are those classic songs. And that's as it should be."},{"cn":"Elisabeth Vincentelli","o":"New York Post","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.nypost.com/p/entertainment/theater/rain_fun_but_it_won_take_you_by_rJcsYQ3qZl7cSbyDc80cLL","q":"It hits all the right notes, but an imitation is still an imitation."},{"cn":"Linda Winer","o":"Newsday","s":49,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.newsday.com/entertainment/theater/rain-less-than-a-broadway-magical-mystery-tour-1.2403861","q":"Everything, alas, except the imagination."},{"cn":"Elisabeth Vincentelli","o":"The New York Times","s":48,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2010/10/27/theater/reviews/27rain.html","q":"This 'Purple Rain,' alas, does not comprehend the power of something we'll never understand."},{"cn":"Jeremy Gerard","o":"Bloomberg","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2010-03-18/hamlet-in-raincoat-bloody-ophelia-where-s-denmark-review","q":"Primarily, however, 'Rain' is a Vegas act for All Hallow's Eve -- a rock horror show."},{"cn":"Matt Windman","o":"amNewYork","s":75,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.amny.com/urbanite-1.812039/rain-not-such-a-fab-four-1.2404286","q":"The homage often feels tired and cheesy, and audience members unwilling to frequently stand up and clap along may be uncomfortable."},{"cn":"Robert Feldberg","o":"NorthJersey.com","s":73,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.northjersey.com/arts_entertainment/105842788_They_put_the_Beatles_on_stage_in_a_theater___and_then_all_you_need_is_love.html","q":"They're quite polished at what they do, which is to ape the Beatles' every intonation and gesture."},{"cn":"Roma Torre","o":"NY1","s":73,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://statenisland.ny1.com/content/ny1_living/theater_reviews/127846/ny1-theater-review---rain-","q":"Rain may not be theatre but it sure is entertaining."},{"cn":"Joe Dziemianowicz","o":"New York Daily News","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.nydailynews.com/2010/10/27/rain-a-tribute-to-the-beatles-review-cheesy-fab-four-sing-alongs-transcend-time/","q":"Your affinity for the Fab Four, cover-band mimicry and bad mop-top wigs will be a good gauge for whether or not this nonstop nostalgia trip is for you."},{"cn":"Elysa Gardner","o":"USA Today","s":57,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.usatoday.com/life/theater/reviews/2010-10-27-rain27_ST_N.htm","q":"Rain is either a new low point or a refreshingly honest enterprise."}],"au":{"score":67,"designation":"Disliking","sources":{"mz":{"s":67,"c":11,"sr":3.4}}},"ta":"250 W 52nd St, New York, NY 10019","pd":"2010-10-19","ca":[{"n":"Joe Bithorn","r":"Vocals, Lead Guitar, Guitar Synth, Sitar"},{"n":"Ralph Castelli","r":"Drums, Percussion, Vocals"},{"n":"Joey Curatolo","r":"Vocals, Bass, Piano, Guitar"},{"n":"Steve Landes","r":"Vocals, Rhythm Guitar, Piano, Harmonica"},{"n":"Mark Beyer","r":"Keyboard, Percussion"},{"n":"Graham Alexander","r":"Vocals, Bass, Piano, Guitar"},{"n":"Joe Bologna","r":"Drums, Percussion, Vocals"},{"n":"Douglas Cox","r":"Drums, Percussion, Vocals"},{"n":"Jim Irizarry","r":"Vocals, Rhythm Guitar, Piano, Harmonica"},{"n":"David Leon","r":"Vocals, Rhythm Guitar, Piano, Harmonica"},{"n":"Mark Lewis","r":"Keyboard, Percussion"},{"n":"Jimmy Pou","r":"Vocals, Lead Guitar, Guitar Synth"},{"n":"Mac Ruffing","r":"Vocals, Bass, Piano, Guitar"},{"n":"Chris Smallwood","r":"Keyboard, Percussion"},{"n":"Tom Teeley","r":"Vocals, Lead Guitar, Guitar Synth, Sitar"}]}